Bootstrap: docker
From: python:3.12-slim

# DockQ v2 -- quality measure for predicted multimers, nucleic acids and
# small-molecule complexes.
#
# NOT BUILT. This recipe has never been run; STATUS in tool.conf is `planned`.
#
# CPU-only and small. No CUDA base, no --nv, no weights: DockQ is arithmetic
# over two structure files, and every other choice here follows from that.
# python:3.12-slim rather than a CUDA image keeps it around 200 MB instead of
# several GB, which matters because this is the one tool in the covalent family
# that will be invoked thousands of times per campaign rather than dozens.
#
# The C-compiler trap DOES NOT APPLY, and the reason is worth stating rather
# than leaving to inference. It bites tools whose GPU kernels are JIT-compiled
# at first use -- boltz's cuequivariance/Triton kernels, DeepSpeed's op
# builder. DockQ has no GPU kernels at all and no JIT path that was found, so
# no compiler is installed. `%post` checks what it got anyway and prints it, so
# that if a future DockQ grows a numba or Cython fast path, the build log says
# so instead of a job finding out. If that day comes, the fix is the same as
# boltz's: a compiler in the image, or NUMBA_CACHE_DIR out of the read-only
# squashfs.
#
# Build:  chpc-tool build dockq          (login node only; /usr/bin/apptainer
#                                         1.5.2, --fakeroot UNAVAILABLE, and
#                                         `module load apptainer` does not
#                                         exist on this cluster)

%labels
    Tool         dockq
    Version      2
    Upstream     https://github.com/bjornwallner/DockQ
    UpstreamRef  DockQ (PyPI) -- pin the exact version at build time
    Licence      MIT
    Base         python:3.12-slim
    Citation     Mirabello and Wallner, Bioinformatics 2024, 10.1093/bioinformatics/btae586
    Maintainer   Craik Lab, UCSF

%post
    set -eux
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    apt-get update
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends ca-certificates
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    pip install --no-cache-dir --upgrade DockQ

    python - <<'PY'
import sys
assert sys.version_info[:2] >= (3, 10), sys.version
print("python", sys.version.split()[0])

import DockQ
print("DockQ", getattr(DockQ, "__version__", "?"))

# Report the JIT situation rather than assume it. Today DockQ is numpy and
# Biopython; if a version grows a numba fast path, a .sif is a read-only
# squashfs and numba refuses at IMPORT time inside one unless NUMBA_CACHE_DIR
# points somewhere writable -- which is how boltz's image failed four seconds
# in, before any input. Printing it costs nothing and turns a future surprise
# into a line in a build log.
import importlib.util
for mod in ("numba", "cython", "triton"):
    print("%-8s %s" % (mod, "present -- see the comment in %post" if importlib.util.find_spec(mod) else "absent"))
for mod in ("numpy", "Bio"):
    spec = importlib.util.find_spec(mod)
    print("%-8s %s" % (mod, "present" if spec else "ABSENT"))
PY
    command -v DockQ

%environment
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
    export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1
    # Set defensively and cheaply: if a future DockQ acquires a numba path,
    # this is the difference between it working inside a read-only squashfs
    # and refusing at import (doc 07). /tmp is bound by apptainer, is local
    # NVMe on every compute node, and is per-node so concurrent array tasks
    # cannot collide over one cache file.
    export NUMBA_CACHE_DIR="${NUMBA_CACHE_DIR:-/tmp/numba-cache}"

%test
    set -eu
    # Against the BUILT, read-only image -- %post runs on a writable overlay,
    # so an import that only fails on squashfs cannot be caught there (doc 07).
    python -c "import DockQ; print('DockQ imports')"
    DockQ --help > /dev/null

%runscript
    exec DockQ "$@"

%help
    DockQ v2 -- Mirabello and Wallner, Bioinformatics 2024.

      chpc-tool exec dockq -- DockQ model.pdb native.pdb --mapping AB:AB --json out.json

    PASS --mapping. Model chains and native chains are different alphabets,
    and DockQ will search chain permutations and report the best one it finds.
    A wrong mapping does not error; it produces a plausible number. In bulk
    scoring that is indistinguishable from a result.

    --small_molecule scores small-molecule poses. Nucleic-acid interfaces are
    scored alongside protein ones.

    CAPRI thresholds: <0.23 Incorrect, 0.23-0.49 Acceptable, 0.49-0.80 Medium,
    >=0.80 High quality.

    CPU only. Send it to the `cpu` partition, or `community_short`, which is
    capped at 1 h and REQUIRES --qos=cmnt_short. It has no business queueing
    behind the gpu partition's 8-GPU, 21-job per-user cap.
